1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,640
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:05,010
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,010 --> 00:00:06,090
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:09,040
I've been a plasterer for
thirty years.

5
00:00:09,090 --> 00:00:10,200
Up on the scaffold,

6
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:11,520
down on my knees,

7
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:13,560
smoothing walls all day.

8
00:00:13,770 --> 00:00:14,740
I had my right knee

9
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:16,310
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:18,700
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:20,440
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:21,700
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:22,830
and it went away.

14
00:00:23,050 --> 00:00:24,050
This is different.

15
00:00:24,330 --> 00:00:24,820
Tight.

16
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:25,510
Full.

17
00:00:25,550 --> 00:00:26,450
Like a band around

18
00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:28,060
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:28,230 --> 00:00:29,260
And for two years I've

20
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:30,550
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:30,870 --> 00:00:31,790
Give it time.

22
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:34,070
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:34,070 --> 00:00:35,370
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:35,650 --> 00:00:36,320
At three months,

25
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:37,310
give it six.

26
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:38,230
At six months,

27
00:00:38,230 --> 00:00:39,860
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:40,660
At a year,

29
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:42,570
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:43,690
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:43,730 --> 00:00:45,070
We went down the list.

32
00:00:45,110 --> 00:00:46,570
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:46,810 --> 00:00:48,070
Every session,

34
00:00:48,070 --> 00:00:49,750
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:51,030
I got stronger.

36
00:00:51,070 --> 00:00:52,430
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:52,470 --> 00:00:54,270
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:54,270 --> 00:00:55,670
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:55,850 --> 00:00:57,720
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:57,720 --> 00:00:58,910
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:58,910 --> 00:01:00,170
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:01:00,420 --> 00:01:02,310
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:04,480
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:07,120
And after that, a second
operation

45
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:07,730
to go back

46
00:01:07,730 --> 00:01:09,370
in and do it over.

47
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:10,750
I said no.

48
00:01:11,010 --> 00:01:13,180
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

49
00:01:13,180 --> 00:01:14,730
and my knee felt like a
band

50
00:01:14,730 --> 00:01:17,750
was wrapped around it,
tightening every inch

51
00:01:17,750 --> 00:01:19,040
I tried to straighten.

52
00:01:19,230 --> 00:01:20,590
Every morning I took
something

53
00:01:20,590 --> 00:01:22,120
for it and went to work.

54
00:01:22,390 --> 00:01:23,840
Couldn't do the stairs,

55
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:24,990
couldn't stand at the
counter

56
00:01:24,990 --> 00:01:26,670
long enough to finish
dinner,

57
00:01:26,670 --> 00:01:28,210
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

58
00:01:28,210 --> 00:01:30,940
game without shifting
every two minutes.

59
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:31,870
At work,

60
00:01:31,870 --> 00:01:34,310
I couldn't climb the
scaffold without stopping,

61
00:01:34,310 --> 00:01:35,360
couldn't kneel to finish

62
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:36,680
the bottom of a wall.

63
00:01:37,020 --> 00:01:38,080
It woke me at night,

64
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:39,630
and it turned ordinary
things,

65
00:01:39,630 --> 00:01:40,950
like getting in the truck

66
00:01:40,950 --> 00:01:42,350
or up off the couch,

67
00:01:42,350 --> 00:01:43,430
into a decision.

68
00:01:43,750 --> 00:01:44,950
After a long and serious

69
00:01:44,950 --> 00:01:46,080
talk with my wife,

70
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:47,650
I went back in one more
time.

71
00:01:47,860 --> 00:01:48,810
That was the fourth set

72
00:01:48,810 --> 00:01:50,150
of X-rays on this knee.

73
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:52,010
And like the three before
it,

74
00:01:52,010 --> 00:01:54,180
the answer was everything
looks great.

75
00:01:54,290 --> 00:01:56,030
No loosening, no
infection,

76
00:01:56,030 --> 00:01:56,870
nothing wrong.

77
00:01:57,030 --> 00:01:58,260
Only this time

78
00:01:58,260 --> 00:01:59,560
there was no new number.

79
00:01:59,690 --> 00:02:01,690
Nobody said give it
another six months.

80
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:03,320
There was nothing left to
give it.

81
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:04,300
I sat in the parking

82
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:05,250
lot for a while.

83
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:06,450
Okay, I thought.

84
00:02:06,490 --> 00:02:07,860
Then explain this.

85
00:02:08,190 --> 00:02:10,310
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

86
00:02:10,310 --> 00:02:11,770
I hit my breaking point.

87
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:14,170
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

88
00:02:14,370 --> 00:02:16,330
Everyone in the house was
asleep

89
00:02:16,330 --> 00:02:18,090
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

90
00:02:18,090 --> 00:02:19,210
with my leg up,

91
00:02:19,210 --> 00:02:20,870
trying to find any angle
where

92
00:02:20,870 --> 00:02:21,990
it didn't feel like
something

93
00:02:21,990 --> 00:02:24,550
was wrapped around my knee
and tightening.

94
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:27,200
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

95
00:02:27,310 --> 00:02:29,170
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

96
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:30,260
I had a ceiling

97
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:31,520
to start at seven.

98
00:02:31,830 --> 00:02:32,700
And I just thought,

99
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:34,440
is this really my life
now?

100
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:36,160
I can't live like this.

101
00:02:36,210 --> 00:02:37,650
Thirty years of walls,

102
00:02:37,650 --> 00:02:38,620
and I didn't know how many

103
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:39,800
more I had in me.

104
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:41,750
So I made myself a
promise.

105
00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:42,640
I wouldn't go a day

106
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:43,990
without looking for an
answer.

107
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:45,480
And when I found one,

108
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:46,670
I'd share it with everyone

109
00:02:46,670 --> 00:02:47,980
going through the same
thing.

110
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:49,100
So I got my laptop

111
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:50,120
out and went looking.

112
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:51,340
Not for a product.

113
00:02:51,440 --> 00:02:52,610
For an explanation.

114
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,520
Mayo Clinic forums,

115
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:56,690
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

116
00:02:56,690 --> 00:02:58,040
doctor videos,

117
00:02:58,040 --> 00:02:59,350
medical animations.

118
00:02:59,730 --> 00:03:00,990
And that's when I found a
video

119
00:03:00,990 --> 00:03:02,660
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

120
00:03:02,700 --> 00:03:04,050
Steven Salinger,

121
00:03:04,050 --> 00:03:05,010
whose own wife had been

122
00:03:05,010 --> 00:03:06,280
through exactly this.

123
00:03:06,450 --> 00:03:07,970
But before I say anything
else,

124
00:03:07,970 --> 00:03:09,630
I want to be straight with
you.

125
00:03:10,110 --> 00:03:12,270
You've already had
something work fast.

126
00:03:12,310 --> 00:03:13,240
The ice.

127
00:03:13,450 --> 00:03:15,230
The first week of a new
pill.

128
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:16,960
The good day after a
session.

129
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:18,490
Then it wore off.

130
00:03:18,620 --> 00:03:20,750
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

131
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:23,100
Fast relief isn't relief.

132
00:03:23,330 --> 00:03:24,270
It's a preview.

133
00:03:24,580 --> 00:03:25,680
So I'm not going to tell

134
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:27,040
you this works fast.

135
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:27,980
It doesn't.

136
00:03:28,170 --> 00:03:30,060
But if you're willing to
be patient,

137
00:03:30,060 --> 00:03:31,250
and to look at what's
going

138
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:32,970
on around your new knee

139
00:03:32,970 --> 00:03:34,520
instead of inside it,
there

140
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:36,860
is a real reason it still
hurts.

141
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:38,960
And something you can do
about it.

142
00:03:39,310 --> 00:03:41,300
Let me explain what he
said,

143
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:42,800
because this is what
changed

144
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:44,180
everything for me.

145
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:46,410
He started with the
basics.

146
00:03:46,630 --> 00:03:48,120
A knee replacement takes
out

147
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,920
the worn joint surfaces

148
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:52,010
and puts in metal and
plastic.

149
00:03:52,250 --> 00:03:54,120
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

150
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,730
you had before the
operation.

151
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:57,740
That part I already knew.

152
00:03:57,950 --> 00:03:59,270
But then he explained
something

153
00:03:59,270 --> 00:04:00,600
nobody had ever told me.

154
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:01,470
He said,

155
00:04:01,470 --> 00:04:02,790
think about a swollen foot

156
00:04:02,790 --> 00:04:03,980
inside a shoe.

157
00:04:04,020 --> 00:04:05,350
The shoe didn't shrink.

158
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:07,740
Your foot is taking up
more room,

159
00:04:07,740 --> 00:04:09,450
so everything feels
cramped

160
00:04:09,450 --> 00:04:10,820
and tight and squeezed.

161
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:12,060
Your new knee sits

162
00:04:12,060 --> 00:04:13,710
in a limited space with
living

163
00:04:13,710 --> 00:04:15,380
tissue packed all around
it.

164
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:17,600
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

165
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:19,450
had to work through that
tissue.

166
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:22,140
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

167
00:04:22,530 --> 00:04:23,950
At first that's normal.

168
00:04:24,390 --> 00:04:26,090
But in some people that
swelling can

169
00:04:26,090 --> 00:04:28,720
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

170
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:30,510
And swollen tissue takes
up more

171
00:04:30,510 --> 00:04:32,300
room than calm tissue
does.

172
00:04:32,350 --> 00:04:33,360
So when you bend,

173
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:35,100
that tissue gets
compressed.

174
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:36,230
When you straighten,

175
00:04:36,230 --> 00:04:37,350
it gets pulled tight.

176
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:38,310
That's the band.

177
00:04:38,350 --> 00:04:40,440
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

178
00:04:40,540 --> 00:04:41,570
And you start being

179
00:04:41,570 --> 00:04:42,850
the one who says,

180
00:04:42,850 --> 00:04:43,580
you go ahead.

181
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:44,650
I'll stay here.

182
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:46,550
And that's exactly why so
much

183
00:04:46,550 --> 00:04:48,320
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

184
00:04:48,730 --> 00:04:50,810
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

185
00:04:50,810 --> 00:04:51,770
around the knee.

186
00:04:52,050 --> 00:04:52,780
Worth doing,

187
00:04:52,780 --> 00:04:53,680
and I'd done it.

188
00:04:53,790 --> 00:04:55,270
It does nothing about
tissue

189
00:04:55,270 --> 00:04:56,380
taking up room.

190
00:04:56,450 --> 00:04:57,650
A nerve block quiets

191
00:04:57,650 --> 00:04:59,320
the nerve carrying the
signal.

192
00:04:59,510 --> 00:05:01,700
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

193
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,760
But when that irritated
tissue

194
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:05,400
finally calms down,

195
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:07,040
it holds less fluid,

196
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:08,650
and it takes up less room.

197
00:05:08,950 --> 00:05:10,740
Less room taken up means

198
00:05:10,740 --> 00:05:12,740
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

199
00:05:12,930 --> 00:05:14,820
That's what takes the
pressure off.

200
00:05:15,180 --> 00:05:16,670
After two years of this,

201
00:05:16,670 --> 00:05:18,270
it finally made sense.

202
00:05:18,610 --> 00:05:20,550
The problem was never the
new knee.

203
00:05:20,690 --> 00:05:22,610
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

204
00:05:22,970 --> 00:05:24,480
He calls it the squeeze.

205
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:27,030
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

206
00:05:27,310 --> 00:05:29,230
I'd bought knee sleeves,

207
00:05:29,230 --> 00:05:32,070
gel knee pads, compression
braces,

208
00:05:32,070 --> 00:05:34,390
creams, half of Amazon
really,

209
00:05:34,390 --> 00:05:35,420
and all any of it gave

210
00:05:35,420 --> 00:05:36,490
me was an hour.

211
00:05:37,010 --> 00:05:37,930
I even looked at going

212
00:05:37,930 --> 00:05:39,860
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

213
00:05:39,990 --> 00:05:42,040
But at $200 a session

214
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:43,580
with nothing covered by
insurance,

215
00:05:43,580 --> 00:05:45,100
that was a quick no.

216
00:05:45,170 --> 00:05:46,500
Then one night I went

217
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:47,780
back to that knee
replacement

218
00:05:47,780 --> 00:05:49,460
group and actually read
it.

219
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:51,150
Thousands of people,

220
00:05:51,150 --> 00:05:53,000
years out from surgery,

221
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,480
comparing notes on
stiffness

222
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:56,530
and tightness nobody could
explain.

223
00:05:56,820 --> 00:05:58,580
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

224
00:05:58,580 --> 00:06:00,550
the same thing kept coming
up.

225
00:06:00,790 --> 00:06:02,430
This one device,

226
00:06:02,430 --> 00:06:04,350
and people saying it was
the first

227
00:06:04,350 --> 00:06:05,770
thing that made a
difference.

228
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:07,910
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

229
00:06:07,910 --> 00:06:09,690
alright, here it comes,

230
00:06:09,690 --> 00:06:11,220
he's selling me something,

231
00:06:11,220 --> 00:06:13,100
let me shut that down
right now.

232
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:15,260
I'm only here because I
made myself

233
00:06:15,260 --> 00:06:17,670
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

234
00:06:17,670 --> 00:06:18,690
that if I ever found

235
00:06:18,690 --> 00:06:19,950
something that helped,

236
00:06:19,950 --> 00:06:21,010
I'd say so.

237
00:06:21,370 --> 00:06:23,230
It's called the KenRelief
Red

238
00:06:23,230 --> 00:06:24,580
Light Therapy Wrap.

239
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:27,210
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

240
00:06:27,460 --> 00:06:29,090
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

241
00:06:29,090 --> 00:06:31,200
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

242
00:06:31,330 --> 00:06:33,370
But I went to their
website anyway,

243
00:06:33,370 --> 00:06:34,220
just to see what all

244
00:06:34,220 --> 00:06:35,310
the fuss was about.

245
00:06:35,630 --> 00:06:37,510
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

246
00:06:37,510 --> 00:06:39,860
charge $200 a session for,

247
00:06:39,860 --> 00:06:42,620
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

248
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:43,560
in a wrap you plug

249
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:44,750
into the wall at home.

250
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:46,460
Two hundred and forty
lights.

251
00:06:46,720 --> 00:06:48,660
Red at 660 nanometers

252
00:06:48,660 --> 00:06:50,810
and near-infrared at 850,

253
00:06:50,810 --> 00:06:53,010
run together for the
strongest effect.

254
00:06:53,210 --> 00:06:54,980
Four strength levels.

255
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:57,190
A five to thirty minute
timer.

256
00:06:57,230 --> 00:06:58,740
Then I saw the guarantee.

257
00:06:58,780 --> 00:06:59,940
Ninety days.

258
00:07:00,010 --> 00:07:02,750
Results or your money
back,

259
00:07:02,750 --> 00:07:05,400
no questions, no store
credit,

260
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:07,030
and you don't even send it
back.

261
00:07:07,250 --> 00:07:09,660
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

262
00:07:09,660 --> 00:07:11,210
days to change my mind.

263
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:12,890
There wasn't much to lose,

264
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:14,070
so I ordered it.

265
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:15,480
Two of them, actually.

266
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:17,690
Only the right knee was
replaced,

267
00:07:17,690 --> 00:07:19,700
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

268
00:07:19,700 --> 00:07:21,440
and I'd done it for two
years.

269
00:07:21,730 --> 00:07:23,740
The left one was carrying
the difference.

270
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:24,680
When it came,

271
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:26,780
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

272
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:27,840
because I'd been let down

273
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:29,670
too many times to get
excited.

274
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:31,450
What I felt was warmth.

275
00:07:31,490 --> 00:07:33,360
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

276
00:07:33,450 --> 00:07:34,990
More like it was coming
from inside

277
00:07:34,990 --> 00:07:36,570
the knee and spreading
around it.

278
00:07:36,810 --> 00:07:37,840
And that was it.

279
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:39,440
That was the whole
experience.

280
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:40,690
When I took it off,

281
00:07:40,690 --> 00:07:41,640
